'''
Mini-Project - Number Guesser
Combine loops, conditionals, user input, and data types to create a simple number guessing game. Hardcode a "secret number" in your script. Use a while loop to continuously prompt the user for a guess. Use if-elif-else conditions to tell the user if their guess is "too high", "too low", or "correct". Break the loop and congratulate the user once they guess correctly.
'''

secret_number = 42

print("Our system have a secret number. can u guess it what it is ?")
while True:
  number = int(input("\nEnter the number - "))
  if (number < secret_number):
    print("Too low! Try the higher number")
  elif (number > secret_number):
    print("Too high! Try the smaller number")
  else:
    print("Congratulation !! You have guess the right number")
    break
